<p>Also worth a visit: the Albert Hall Museum, a striking building that is lit up in the evening.</p></section>

<section class="st" id="do" style="--lc:var(--or)"><h2>Things to Do in Jaipur</h2>
<p>Jaipur is as much about markets and craft as monuments.</p>
<ul class="chips"><li>Block-printed textiles</li><li>Blue pottery</li><li>Jewellery and gemstones</li><li>Leather juttis</li><li>Guided old city walk</li><li>Cooking class</li><li>Sunset at Patrika Gate</li><li>Hot-air balloon at Amber</li></ul>
<div class="note">Look for shops in Johari Bazaar, Bapu Bazaar and Tripolia Bazaar. A balloon flight over the Amber area is an option in cooler months.</div></section>

<section class="st" id="reach" style="--lc:var(--y)"><h2>How to Reach Jaipur from Delhi</h2>
<p>Jaipur is about 280 km from Delhi, and there are four ways to get there.</p>
<div class="grid"><div><h3>Train</h3><p>Fast services take around 4.5 to 5 hours with several daily departures. A comfortable and affordable choice.</p></div><div><h3>Road</h3><p>The highway drive takes about 5 to 6 hours depending on traffic. A private car suits families and groups.</p></div><div><h3>Bus</h3><p>Air-conditioned and Volvo buses run from Delhi at lower cost.</p></div><div><h3>Air</h3><p>Jaipur International Airport has flights from Delhi, Mumbai and other cities.</p></div></div>
<div class="note">Travel times are approximate. Check current train timings and book on the official IRCTC website: <a href="https://www.irctc.co.in/" rel="noopener">https://www.irctc.co.in/</a></div></section>

<section class="st" id="stay" style="--lc:var(--vi)"><h2>Where to Stay in Jaipur</h2>
<p>Jaipur is known for heritage hotels in restored palaces and havelis, alongside budget and mid-range options.</p>
<div class="grid"><div><h3>Old City (Pink City)</h3><p>Close to the palaces and bazaars, with heritage havelis and small hotels.</p></div><div><h3>C-Scheme</h3><p>A central, modern area with restaurants, cafés and good transport links.</p></div><div><h3>Civil Lines and Bani Park</h3><p>Quieter residential areas with boutique hotels and guesthouses.</p></div><div><h3>Amer Road</h3><p>Near Amber Fort, with several palace-style hotels.</p></div></div>
<p>Check guest reviews, distance to the main sights, breakfast and cancellation policy before booking, and book early from October to March.</p></section>

<section class="st" id="itinerary" style="--lc:var(--rd)"><h2>Two-Day Jaipur Itinerary</h2>
<p>Two days cover the main forts, palaces and bazaars.</p>
<ol class="days"><li><b>Day 1 morning:</b> Amber Fort, then a photo stop at Jal Mahal.</li><li><b>Day 1 afternoon:</b> City Palace and Jantar Mantar.</li><li><b>Day 1 evening:</b> Hawa Mahal and the old bazaars.</li><li><b>Day 2 morning:</b> Nahargarh or Jaigarh Fort.</li><li><b>Day 2 midday:</b> Albert Hall Museum.</li><li><b>Day 2 afternoon:</b> shopping for textiles and crafts.</li><li><b>Day 2 sunset:</b> Nahargarh or Patrika Gate.</li></ol></section>

<section class="st" id="food" style="--lc:var(--pk)"><h2>Jaipur Food and Shopping</h2>
<p>Try dal baati churma, laal maas, ghewar, pyaaz kachori and lassi. Look for block-printed fabric, gemstones, blue pottery, juttis and Rajasthani puppets.</p>
<ul class="chips"><li>Dal baati churma</li><li>Laal maas</li><li>Ghewar</li><li>Pyaaz kachori</li><li>Lassi</li><li>Block prints</li><li>Blue pottery</li><li>Juttis</li></ul>
<div class="note">Agree prices before buying, and choose busy, clean restaurants.</div></section>

<section class="st" id="safety" style="--lc:var(--gr)"><h2>Safety and Travel Tips</h2>
<p>Jaipur is a major tourist city, so take normal precautions.</p>
<ul class="l"><li>Use trusted taxis or app-based cabs, and agree rickshaw fares first.</li><li>Be cautious of anyone offering a special shop visit, as commissions can raise prices.</li><li>Drink sealed or purified water.</li><li>Dress modestly at temples.</li><li>Carry sun protection in summer.</li><li>At Amber Fort, consider walking or taking a jeep up instead of an elephant ride, as many travellers now prefer to avoid animal rides.</li></ul></section>

